{
 "code_list": "valve_type",
 "version": "1.3.1",
 "description": "WI valve type. isolates: the valve is an isolation valve - closed for a mains repair and in isolation analysis (rule R4).",
 "attributes": {
  "isolates": "isolation valve: closed for a mains repair and in isolation analysis; stops an isolation trace. Rule (James 14/10/2026, reverts 13/10 'a valve is a valve'): only isolation valves (sluice / gate, butterfly line valve, boundary, district, motorised) isolate. PRV / PSV / flow control / pressure breaking / float are control valves that pass water backwards; a non-return valve is no reverse isolation; washout, air and stop tap are off the main; other / blank = unknown type, not an isolation valve. Matches what the Synergi isolation scripts close (VL valves only) and the legacy readers' gate valves."
 },
